<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Recklinghausen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Recklinghausen is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhr">Ruhr area</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From the 13th century it was the centre of the Vest Recklinghausen, an outlying territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/electorate-of-cologne">Electorate of Cologne</a>, which passed to the Duke of Arenberg in 1803 and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1815. In the 19th and 20th centuries it grew with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mining.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/recklinghausen.jpg" alt="Recklinghausen" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dietmar Rabich · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Recklinghausen,_Rathaus_--_2015_--_7398.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
